<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-explicit-binding> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Bind each process-control instance to one explicit versioned profile selector, repository-relative manifest selector, through boundary, tracked automation-policy digest and exact lifecycle-tool digest before provider contact; keep global semantic revision and per-work scoped dependency digests as dynamic observations so graph movement rederives only affected work without whole-process restart or reproof." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-unix-foreground> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-unix-foreground> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep the composer foreground and JSONL-composable; use an explicit Linux util-linux flock instance boundary whose descriptor is released by process death, while ordinary Unix supervision owns backgrounding, restart and forced termination rather than a USF daemon, socket or service manager." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-safe-stop-restart> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-safe-stop-restart> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use an OS-released exact-instance ownership lock and nonce-bound graceful-stop intent, retain ownership while any admitted work survives the drain bound, reject ambiguous identity and recover a killed process by stale quarantine and current-state rescan without replay." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-nonauthority> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-nonauthority> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Treat lifecycle files as disposable operational observations that grant no work-completion, integration, evidence, proof or publication authority." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-remote-independent> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:lifecycle-remote-independent> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Require no GitHub or Git-remote access for start, watch, stop or through-check progress; keep local carrier identity, coherent commit batching and explicit push separate so remote unavailability cannot block unrelated local work." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:foreground-lifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:foreground-lifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Foreground start, JSONL readiness, idempotent and concurrent start, instance-bound stop, SIGINT/SIGTERM drain, stale restart, unrelated semantic movement preservation and planted malformed or mismatched identity cases have deterministic outcomes without PID-only signalling or whole-graph reproof." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
