<urn:usf:requirement:operator-help-registry> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use one static command registry for parsing and help; render human help and stable JSON help without repository, GitHub, provider, supervisor or network access, including synopsis, options, schema, exit codes, availability, external contact, history scan and authority effects." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-metrics-bounded> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-metrics-bounded> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Implement status as a cheap current summary and metrics as a bounded aggregate over explicit JSONL or ignored local operational records with source coverage, filters, limits, truncation and no unbounded scan or label cardinality; reserve observe as a distinct planned point-in-time command for later graph-defined work." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-metrics-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-metrics-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Separate requested route, actual provider and underlying model denominators; distinguish unknown from zero; count useful tokens only when exact accepted candidate, review, repair or proof lineage names the contribution." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-metrics-nonauthority> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-metrics-nonauthority> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Make help, status and metrics local and read-only with no provider or remote contact, implicit probe, semantic mutation, commit or push; exclude prompts, responses, credentials, endpoints, absolute paths and unbounded labels from events and output." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:requirement:operator-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep one registry/help contract, table-driven pure aggregation coverage and one subprocess boundary; retain named no-force-exit lanes, map every test to a unique risk and prune duplicates rather than growing repeated matrices; clean-clone tests recreate ignored local cache fixtures and require neither a warm CAS nor a self-hosted GitHub runner." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:operator-observability> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:operator-observability> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Help works outside a repository; status remains a broad bounded summary; all metric views have stable JSON, filters, coverage and denominators; planted unknown, truncation, identity and useful-lineage cases remain factual and local-only." <urn:usf:graph:usf-bootstrap> .
